# Every text file is LF in the working tree on every machine (AI-34, 2026-10-01).
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system gitconfig, so without
# this a Windows clone checks text out as CRLF while CI's Linux checkout is LF.
# The index was already all LF; this only changes what Windows writes to disk.
# Suites and guards read source files and search them for a newline followed by "}":
# schedule-browser/smoke-dark-theme failed on Windows alone because of it, and
# would have been the first of several. text=auto still leaves binaries alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Path 21 art: SVG is text and must hash the same on every checkout, so it is
# kept LF in the working tree even with core.autocrlf=true. The validator also
# strips CR before hashing SVG; this makes the file on disk match as well.
assets/art/**/*.svg text eol=lf
Tools/*/art/**/*.svg text eol=lf
Tools/blender-art/renders.json text eol=lf
*.webp binary
assets/art/**/*.png binary
